A||N||1||fropuff||The ghetto cruiser needs help!!!||||8||
Z||000000||fropuff||09-23-2000||04:37 PM||||Hey, I just finished putting my temperature gauge in my 80 Cutlass.  I started it up, and it sounds like CRAP!  I'll tell you the story...<BR>Last weekend, I decided to change the valve cover gaskets.  They were BAD!  One piece was missing at the "dog ear" piece, which was causing my leak.  Okay, I started it after that and took it for a short spin.  Ran about the same, maybe a little better.  Then, I decided to change the fuel filter.  On this particular vehicle, the filter is located in by the gas line by the intake?  and goes to the carb.  I replaced it, and as I was trying to put it back in, I noticed that the gas line broke!  When I was loosening, or at least though I was loosening, the assembly, the gas line twisted with the assembly until it broke, which was when it came off.  My grandpa and I sawed off the broken end and took out the piece that was on the assembly.  We took a 1 1/2" piece off the "good" side, and put it on the assembly.  We connected the two with a 3/8" rubber tube.  Clamped both ends off.  Worked real good.  My brother was putting the assembly back into the carb and cross-threaded the thing.  He put it all the way in, so I thought it would work.  I put the air filter assembly back on.  I got the temperature gauge done today, so I started it for the first time in a week.  MAN, does it sound like CRAP!  Tickin' and crap.  I also saw that gas was leaking from, guess where, the filter.  What is causing this?  I'm sorry that it's so long, I just wanted to tell you everything.  New engine?  Thanks.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000001||fropuff||09-23-2000||04:40 PM||||Oh, it also "ticks" faster as I rev it up.  I changed the oil and filter last weekend as well.  The engine almost dies when I have it in gear and my foot on the brake.  Thanks again.||||reg||1
